## Summary

Both DeepSeek API models fail the `tool calling` compatibility check. DeepSeek rejects a forced `tool_choice` while thinking mode is enabled, and the `deepseek-thinking` request profile enables thinking unconditionally without downgrading `tool_choice`.

```
$ ./bin/test-model 'deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash' --live --yes
PASS basic response
PASS streaming: stream text and completion event verified
FAIL tool calling: deepseek rejected the request for DeepSeek V4 Flash (API).
     (HTTP 400: Thinking mode does not support this tool_choice)
PASS compaction: compaction response verified
```

`deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` fails identically.

## Root cause

`src/api-forwarder.mjs`, the `deepseek-thinking` branch sets `payload.thinking = { type: "enabled" }` but leaves `tool_choice` untouched:

```js
} else if (model.requestProfile === "deepseek-thinking") {
  payload.thinking = { type: "enabled" };
  payload.reasoning_effort = deepSeekEffort(payload.reasoning_effort);
  delete payload.temperature;
  delete payload.top_p;
  delete payload.presence_penalty;
  delete payload.frequency_penalty;
}
```

The `qwen-plan` branch a few lines below already carries the guard for the identical upstream restriction, quoting the same error text:

```js
// Qwen rejects forced tool choices in thinking mode
// ("tool_choice ... does not support being set to required or object");
// downgrade to auto so tool calls stay available.
if (payload.tool_choice !== undefined && payload.tool_choice !== "none") {
  payload.tool_choice = "auto";
}
```

Qwen Plan resells DeepSeek, which is likely where the restriction was first hit — the fix landed on that path only.

## Impact

Not limited to the compatibility test (`src/compatibility-test.mjs` sends `tool_choice: "required"`). `src/router.mjs` sends `tool_choice` as an **object** for the agent payload relay, so **routed subagents on any DeepSeek-thinking model fail** in normal use, not just under `test-model`.

## Proposed fix

Mirror the existing guard into the `deepseek-thinking` branch:

```diff
   } else if (model.requestProfile === "deepseek-thinking") {
     payload.thinking = { type: "enabled" };
     payload.reasoning_effort = deepSeekEffort(payload.reasoning_effort);
     delete payload.temperature;
     delete payload.top_p;
     delete payload.presence_penalty;
     delete payload.frequency_penalty;
+    // DeepSeek rejects forced tool choices in thinking mode
+    // ("Thinking mode does not support this tool_choice");
+    // downgrade to auto so tool calls stay available.
+    if (payload.tool_choice !== undefined && payload.tool_choice !== "none") {
+      payload.tool_choice = "auto";
+    }
   } else if (model.requestProfile === "deepseek-nonthinking") {
```

Verified locally — with this applied, all four checks pass on both models:

```
DeepSeek V4 Flash (API)   basic PASS  streaming PASS  tool calling PASS  compaction PASS
DeepSeek V4 Pro   (API)   basic PASS  streaming PASS  tool calling PASS  compaction PASS
```

Happy to open a PR if you'd prefer that over the inline diff.

