### Requested correction and validation

Recognize the effective native Responses Lite tool declarations while honoring explicit tool restrictions and keeping ordinary native and third-party routed behavior intact. Preserve the existing durable-commit and signed, unexpired conversation/permission-scoped readback requirements. Missing tools, denied access, failed writes, or invalid proofs must keep the complete text; past shell execution alone must not authorize omission.

The existing pure aging-policy suite passed 55/55 (`node --test test/tool-result-aging.test.mjs`). In-memory negative controls also preserved full text for explicit empty tools, disabled tool choice, forced unrelated tools, the newest-four frontier, and absence of a later model action.

A fix should add mock client/provider coverage for native omitted-top-level-tools requests, explicit capability removal, storage/readback failures, valid and invalid proofs, and unchanged routed behavior. This investigation applied no fix and did not restart the running router. Archive-writing and full router integration tests were not rerun; end-to-end archival/readback and positive savings remain unverified.

